==German==

===Etymology===
Probably related to Indo-European ''*sker-a-'' "to [[cut]]", which is related to [[scheren]]. Akin to English {{term|shard|lang=en}}, Old Norse {{term|skarð||notch, hack|lang=non}} ( > Danish {{term|skår|lang=da}}).

